---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How the Ownpremise website handles your data: no cookies, no third-party analytics, no third-party scripts, and what happens when you email us."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="num">00</span>Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy notice.</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 1rem">
        This notice covers the website at ownpremise.com. It is short because the site does very
        little with your data.
      </p>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 1rem; font-size: 0.9375rem">Last updated: 22 October 2026.</p>

      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        The website is operated by StackSolver UK Limited, Company No. 16227080, registered office at
        215 Ditchling Road, Brighton BN1 6JD, United Kingdom. For the purposes of UK data protection
        law, StackSolver UK Limited is the controller of any personal data described in this notice.
      </p>

      <h2>What this website does not do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>It sets no cookies, first-party or third-party.</li>
        <li>It uses no analytics service, third-party or otherwise.</li>
        <li>It loads no scripts, fonts, images or styles from any other domain. Everything is served from ownpremise.com.</li>
        <li>It has no contact form. There is nothing on this site that submits your data to a third party.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Server logs</h2>
      <p>
        Like any website, this one is served by a hosting provider that keeps standard server logs:
        the address your request came from, the page requested, the time, and the browser identifier
        your software sends. We use those logs only to keep the site running and secure. We do not
        combine them with any other data and we do not use them to identify visitors. They are kept for
        the provider's standard retention period and then deleted.
      </p>

      <h2>When you email us</h2>
      <p>
        The contact links on this site open your own email client with our address filled in. Your
        email provider, not this website, transmits the message. We receive whatever you send: your
        address, your name if your client includes it, and the content of the message.
      </p>
      <p>
        We use that information to reply to you and, if the conversation continues, as a record of the
        enquiry. The legal basis is our legitimate interest in responding to people who write to us.
        We keep enquiries for 24 months after the last message, unless a contract or an evaluation
        follows, in which case the correspondence is kept for as long as that relationship and the
        law require.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not sell or share your details. If you ask us to introduce you to a partner in your
        region, we will pass on your message and your address to that partner, and we will tell you
        we have done so.
      </p>

      <h2>If a form is added</h2>
      <p>
        There is no form on this site today. If one is added, this notice will be updated before it
        goes live to say what the form collects and where it goes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under UK data protection law you can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you,
        ask us to correct or delete it, and object to our use of it. Write to
        <a href="mailto:hello@stacksolveruk.com?subject=Data%20protection">hello@stacksolveruk.com</a>
        or to the registered office above. If you are not satisfied with our answer, you can complain to
        the Information Commissioner's Office at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        If this notice changes, the date at the top changes with it. We do not announce changes any
        other way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
